(487, 'shiva-gujarat-koteshwar-narayan-sarovar-koteshwar-mahadev', 'shiva', 'Koteshwar Mahadev', NULL, 'Gujarat', 'Koteshwar (Narayan Sarovar)', 'Kutch district', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'Koteshwar is a small village and the location of an ancient Shiva temple. It located near the mouth of Kori Creek, in the west of  Kutch district of Gujarat, India.
In past, the temple was almost entirely cut off from the mainland by tidal creeks but now is connected by road. Koteshwar Mahady is said to be the Bhairava of Hinglaj Mata residing at Hinglaj.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Koteshwar_Mahadev_Temple%2C_Kutch%2C_Gujarat_1.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Koteshwar_Mahadev_Temple,_Kutch,_Gujarat_1.jpg', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["Shiva Temple","Gujarat"]', '["Not Available"]', '["Maha Shivaratri"]', 'Koteshwar is a small village and the location of an ancient Shiva temple. It located near the mouth of Kori Creek, in the west of  Kutch district of Gujarat, India.
