(1991, 'shiva-madhya-pradesh-ujjain-siddhavat-temple', 'shiva', 'Siddhavat Temple', NULL, 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Ujjain', 'Kshipra River', 'Shiva', 'Shaiva', 'A sacred riverside temple area associated with ancestral rites and a revered banyan tree.', NULL, 'Rituals by the Kshipra and the ancient banyan.', NULL, 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ram_Ghat,_Ujjain_01.jpg', 'Wikimedia Commons', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram_Ghat,_Ujjain_01.jpg', 'Early morning during river rituals.', 'Open daily; timings vary by season.', 'Modest attire recommended.', 'Footwear is not allowed inside temple areas.', '["Riverbank","Pilgrimage","Rituals"]', '["Daily puja"]', '["Kumbh period","Mahashivratri"]', 'Ujjain district tourism describes Siddhavat as a siddh place on the Shipra and links it to the sacred banyan tradition, comparing it to the Akshay Vat at Prayag.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Ujjain traditions place Siddhavat among the sacred banyans of India and narrate that the vat tree here was planted and worshipped by Parvati. The site is treated as a paapmochan tirtha where rites like shraddha, pind daan, and tarpan are believed to yield special merit.', 'Nath sadhus continue to worship here, and the riverside rituals keep the place active through the year. Siddhavat is also remembered as a key Kshipra bank for ancestral rites during Kumbh cycles.', '[{"label":"Places of Interest (Siddhavat)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/places-of-interest/","type":"Government tourism"},{"label":"Siddhwat Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siddhwat_Temple","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Places of Interest (Siddhavat)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/places-of-interest/","type":"Government tourism"},{"label":"Siddhwat Temple","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siddhwat_Temple","type":"Encyclopedia"}]', '[{"label":"Places of Interest (Ujjain district)","url":"https://ujjain.nic.in/en/places-of-interest/"}]', 3, 'seed', 'Places of Interest (U